Converted from [SourceForge issue 1644559](http://sourceforge.net/support/tracker.php?aid=1644559), submitted by easirois

The Toolkit has dependency on the Catalogmanager.properties file to be in the classpath. The properties file helps the CatalogResolver find the proper XML catalog for the DTD and XML Schemas. In the Java code, since it knows where the catalog file catalog-dita.xml is located, the Java code should programatically point to the location and setup the CatalogManager in Java rather than depending on the system knowing the whereabouts the CatalogManager.properties file is located.

Also, we cannot guarantee that there are other CatalogManager.properties available on the system thus leaving it up to the resolver to pick which propeties file to use.

Thanks to Hussein Shafie from XMLMind with this issue!

Eric

